{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction","id":445315,"title":"Primal Urge re: Feeding Restriction","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-16T21:29:38-07:00","id":445315,"title":"Primal Urge re: Feeding Restriction","content":"If I'm reading this correctly, once a Werewolf hits Primal Urge 2, her feeding restriction becomes meat. Does that mean she can ONLY eat meat from then on? She cannot digest any other form of lipids, carbs, or protein besides meat?<br /> <br /> Maybe it's because I'm going through a section of schooling that's dealing with the act of digestion and what we get from our food (and the test is giving me anxiety beyond belief), this detailing of dietary restriction is really puzzling and vague.<br /> <br /> Is it a spiritual sustenance that needs the act of devouring meat? A la, you lose essence if you don't imbibe in eating meat because you're ignoring the spirit-wolf half? Or is it the physical G.I tract that can no longer develop the enzymes required for anything other than protein breakdown (and even then, does the G.I tract somehow know if the werewolf snuck in a sushi roll?) and what then? Does the werewolf vomit up what they can't digest?<br /> <br /> This sounds pedantic, but it's actually something that once I noticed it, I couldn't let it go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T21:36:33-07:00","id":445340,"title":"","content":"You can only gain sustenance from the type of food you are restricted to (yes there is a supernatural aspect to it). You can eat veggies if you want a case of the shits, but that's all you're going to get from eating them..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T21:36:42-07:00","id":445342,"title":"","content":"Sorry. According to <b>Page 93</b>, you cannot digest Fats, Oils, Sweets, Milk, Yogurt, Cheese, Dry Beans, Eggs, Nuts, Vegetables, Fruits, Bread, Cereal, Rice or Pasta. =D<br /> <br /> In other words:<br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/JyKPhCs.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 03-17-2015, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T21:42:45-07:00","id":445344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445340#post445340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can only gain sustenance from the type of food you are restricted to (yes there is a supernatural aspect to it). You can eat veggies if you want a case of the shits, but that's all you're going to get from eating them..</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes absolutely no sense on the physical side of things. Vampires and blood ... ok, I can suspend my disbelief for that. Saying that only eating meat on a daily basis can even allow a wolf to maintain their essence stores? Sure, no problem.<br /> But I did not slave away at memorizing the Krebs Cycle for Werewolves to laugh in the face of basic biology. &gt;:[<br /> <br /> Now I'm picturing a werewolf's digestive system gaining semi-awareness and having a checklist for what's ok to break down. That vension? Sure. Big Mac? ....we'll let it slide. Tofu-burger? You're getting the shits there, mac, thinking you could slip one past us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 03-17-2015, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T21:45:51-07:00","id":445347,"title":"","content":"Like Darksider said, you *can* eat things other than meat, but you don't gain any nourishment from doing so. The reason for this is probably supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T21:52:29-07:00","id":445353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445347#post445347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Darksider said, you *can* eat things other than meat, but you don't gain any nourishment from doing so. The reason for this is probably supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but the consequences are a bloated tummy, vomiting after every meal, or a bad case of the shits.<br /> Which coincidentally is a much tighter restriction than a wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T21:54:40-07:00","id":445359,"title":"","content":"They aren't really wolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T22:05:08-07:00","id":445367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445344#post445344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This makes absolutely no sense on the physical side of things. Vampires and blood ... ok, I can suspend my disbelief for that. Saying that only eating meat on a daily basis can even allow a wolf to maintain their essence stores? Sure, no problem.<br /> But I did not slave away at memorizing the Krebs Cycle for Werewolves to laugh in the face of basic biology. &gt;:[<br /> <br /> Now I'm picturing a werewolf's digestive system gaining semi-awareness and having a checklist for what's ok to break down. That vension? Sure. Big Mac? ....we'll let it slide. Tofu-burger? You're getting the shits there, mac, thinking you could slip one past us.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be too worried about &quot;basic biology&quot; concerning RPG game characters who change shape at will, talk to spirits and would be totally unfazed dealing with vampires, wizards and other supernatural creatures. Primal dietary restrictions are far lower on the werewolf concern scale than more essential scientific matters like conservation of mass. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T22:15:35-07:00","id":445369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445367#post445367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't be too worried about &quot;basic biology&quot; concerning RPG game characters who change shape at will, talk to spirits and would be totally unfazed dealing with vampires, wizards and other supernatural creatures. Primal dietary restrictions are far lower on the werewolf concern scale than more essential scientific matters like conservation of mass. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It does create some concerns when you have to pretend to be human and sit down to dinner with others.<br /> And have to excuse yourself to the bathroom after every meal.<br /> And it makes me wonder how they get vitamins and trace minerals.<br /> Or if they are immune to most ingested poisons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T22:19:33-07:00","id":445370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445367#post445367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't be too worried about &quot;basic biology&quot; concerning RPG game characters who change shape at will, talk to spirits and would be totally unfazed dealing with vampires, wizards and other supernatural creatures. Primal dietary restrictions are far lower on the werewolf concern scale than more essential scientific matters like conservation of mass. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You would think so, but shapeshifting and gifts don't concern me as much as something so silly and simple as why a werewolf who is supposed to be at the peak of human perfection at the first change will now and forever get horribly sick when they decide to go out for ice cream on a summer day. For my own sanity I'm probably just going to houserule werewolves having to eat in regards to their restrictions to gain/keep Essence and other foods won't supply that spiritual nourishment but biologically, they'll be fine if they decide to stay vegetarian for a day.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T22:28:58-07:00","id":445373,"title":"","content":"Werewolves aren't supposed to be the peak of human perfection. They're not even technically human. What they are is the peak of predatory perfection, and part of that is not eating things you don't have to hunt first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T22:40:52-07:00","id":445391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445373#post445373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves aren't supposed to be the peak of human perfection.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think she means the way <i>'the First Change perfects any existing imperfections.'</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T22:47:05-07:00","id":445394,"title":"","content":"@<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax\">Incendax</a> and @<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie\">Aynie</a>: As Charlaquin correctly notes, werewolves are not (or at least are no longer) human. They are supernatural predators that are effectively half-spirit. Trying to fit human norms, no less hard science facts, to their biology and psychology is futile, unnecessary and often counterproductive to the themes of the game. For instance, given the amount of mass that would be necessary for a werewolf to consume to be able to constantly change shape and regenerate would leave them little time to do anything but constantly eat? As mentioned earlier, if you are sufficiently comfortable with the suspension of disbelief necessary for werewolves to even exist (and vampire, mages, spirits, changelings, etc.), the focus on the peculiarities of their diet as if they were human seems somewhat picayune.<br /> <br /> Note also that a werewolf explicitly can eat all human food, but as stated on p. 93, &quot;While she can ingest other foods she cannot gain nourishment from them, and loses a point of Essence each day that she goes without.&quot; Nourishment, in this instance, and unlike regular humans, is both physical and spiritual. There is no indication that their supernatural biology requires them to constantly purge everything that doesn't nourish them (unlike vampires and real food).<br /> <br /> The book also explicitly deals with werewolves' level of immunity to toxins and disease on p. 95.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T22:54:35-07:00","id":445398,"title":"","content":"I think this is being over-thought.<br /> <br /> Werewolves quickly become obligate carnivores (something the book specifies directly). Obligate carnivores exist in nature without massive digestive issues. They can consume material that isn't meat, even if they don't digest it fully, without negative health effects (and sometimes it is beneficial for them to do so). They get all the nutrients they need from the flesh of other animals who have those nutrients in their flesh already.<br /> <br /> Nothing in the book says that a werewolf that eats ice-cream is going to vomit or have diarrhea because of it. It says eating it doesn't do anything. And even if you for some reason wanted to treat such things as mild toxins, werewolves subtract their Primal Urge from the toxicity rating of toxins... so they'd pretty much never suffer from minor toxins from eating restrictions anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T23:07:54-07:00","id":445404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445398#post445398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is being over-thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do want to clarify that I am approaching this as being a <i>hilarious</i> situation. I hope my comedic image helps convey that. Never at my own table would I be so pedantic to care about the consequences of a Werewolf eating pasta. For me, it is only important from a spiritual perspective that they eat some meat (of the designated variety).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445398#post445398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing in the book says that a werewolf that eats ice-cream is going to vomit or have diarrhea because of it. It says eating it doesn't do anything. And even if you for some reason wanted to treat such things as mild toxins, werewolves subtract their Primal Urge from the toxicity rating of toxins... so they'd pretty much never suffer from minor toxins from eating restrictions anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>But here is where the <i>comedy</i> comes in. On Page 93 it explicitly states that she can &quot;<u><i><b>ONLY DIGEST MEAT</b></i></u>&quot;.<br /> This creates some absolutely knee slapping implications. It is really fun (for me) to speculate about the implications.<br /> Especially since vomiting food was actually a social issue in Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T00:30:35-07:00","id":445427,"title":"","content":"I appreciate that you're coming at this from a specific angle... but you're not the only person in the conversation.<br /> <br /> It's also really disingenuous to keep citing a single phrase from p. 93 completely out of context. It only has humorous implications if you ignore the rest of the sentence around it, ignore the sentences after it, and ignore what the word digest actually means in a biological context.<br /> <br /> Saying something can only digest meat doesn't mean it cannot ingest grains, and process grains through the digestive tract. It means that thing cannot convert grains into a material that can be absorbed through its digestive organs to be processed into nutrients for the body. The whole big reason people stress things like having more fiber and whole grains in your diet is actually because of the stuff you <i>can't</i> digest. Those indigestible parts of grains actually aid normal human digestion and excretion. For a normal person it's the people that don't eat indigestible food that have &quot;knee-slapping&quot; implications from their diets; not the other way around.<br /> <br /> It's also worth remembering that some people just aren't going to find, &quot;eating this makes you violently ill!&quot; funny; especially if you're twisting the wording of the text so hard just to make a poop joke.<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445370#post445370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my own sanity I'm probably just going to houserule werewolves having to eat in regards to their restrictions to gain/keep Essence and other foods won't supply that spiritual nourishment but biologically, they'll be fine if they decide to stay vegetarian for a day.</div> </div> </div> </div>You realize that you basically don't need this to be a house rule?<br /> <br /> A werewolf can go Stamina + Resolve days (basic WOD Deprivation rules) before they'd suffer any ill-effects from not consuming enough of their current feeding restriction before biological starvation would set in. If they go vegetarian for a few days is isn't going to do anything by the rules already besides mess with their Essence; which you aren't intending to house-rule away as it is. The Essence tax side of it is so much harsher than the biological starvation side of it, that worrying about the biological starvation side is practically pointless.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are predators. The game rules reinforce that. The game rules aren't so harsh as you seem to be reading them, so most PCs really never have to worry about this. This is only really going to be an issue if you're purposefully playing a character that's struggling against their predator nature; at which point the systems punishing them is sort of the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T00:51:03-07:00","id":445433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445344#post445344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I did not slave away at memorizing the Krebs Cycle for Werewolves to laugh in the face of basic biology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes you did. You may have also learned about human anatomy for werewolves to shapeshift and laugh in the face of basic biology. You may have learned about cell division, healing pathways and scarring, for werewolves to regenerate and laugh in the face of basic biology.<br /> <br /> High PU werewolves have an increasingly restricted diet. It's part of the price they pay for being half spirit supernatural creatures. They're not human. They don't follow all human-understood scientific laws. <br /> <br /> They can eat other things, they don't gain sustenance from them. That's it. I think it's explained clearly on p 93.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T00:59:16-07:00","id":445440,"title":"","content":"So high primal urge high harmony wolves = cannibals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T01:01:12-07:00","id":445441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445440#post445440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So high primal urge high harmony wolves = cannibals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not by definition, but it's going to be difficult for them to find other easy sources of essence. :-/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T02:29:02-07:00","id":445535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445440#post445440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So high primal urge high harmony wolves = cannibals?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you mean the Primal Urge 8-10 Uratha have Essence restriction, they should be able to eat spirits also. You just need to call the <i>Siskur-Dah</i> every day to eat some spirits. Yes, <i>Hisil</i> will hate high PU werewolves...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T02:37:03-07:00","id":445540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445535#post445535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you mean the Primal Urge 8-10 Uratha have Essence restriction, they should be able to eat spirits also. You just need to call the <i>Siskur-Dah</i> every day to eat some spirits. Yes, <i>Hisil</i> will hate high PU werewolves...</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't have to eat all the Essence and kill the spirit mind you. Besides they can also get it from a locus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T02:45:45-07:00","id":445545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445398#post445398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is being over-thought.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>It definitely is. I'm currently in the middle of cramming for a big biochemistry test and was answering a question for a friend for Primal Urge and noticed the Feeding Restriction and it was approps to my current interests.<br /> <br /> is the biological aspects causing me to twitch with the implications? Yeah, but I'm probably not going to ever touch on it in an actual game. I'm not <i>that</i> crazy<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445427#post445427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You realize that you basically don't need this to be a house rule?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I would if I wanted to not include physical starvation as a part and parcel of the wolfy condition but I do see where you're coming from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445433#post445433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes you did. You may have also learned about human anatomy for werewolves to shapeshift and laugh in the face of basic biology. You may have learned about cell division, healing pathways and scarring, for werewolves to regenerate and laugh in the face of basic biology.<br /> <br /> High PU werewolves have an increasingly restricted diet. It's part of the price they pay for being half spirit supernatural creatures. They're not human. They don't follow all human-understood scientific laws.<br /> <br /> They can eat other things, they don't gain sustenance from them. That's it. I think it's explained clearly on p 93.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was more of a exasperated amusement sort of musing than any actual critique towards the game. As for the regeneration and shapeshifting, those parts don't trigger a &quot;this is really weird&quot; thing for me.<br /> <br /> Werewolves being unable to digest anything beyond meat did bug me and I was curious on if the restriction was actually physical in nature or just a hindrance towards maintaining a spiritual health/balance sort of deal. As several of you have confirmed it was a physical restriction, I'm gonna thank you all for the answers and go on my merry way to consider that for my own games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 03-17-2015, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T02:55:45-07:00","id":445547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445545#post445545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It definitely is. I'm currently in the middle of cramming for a big biochemistry test and was answering a question for a friend for Primal Urge and noticed the Feeding Restriction and it was approps to my current interests.</div> </div> </div> </div>Best of luck for the exams. Biochemistry can be hard to get one's head around <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T03:02:35-07:00","id":445549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445427#post445427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also really disingenuous to keep citing a single phrase from p. 93 completely out of context. It only has humorous implications if you ignore the rest of the sentence around it, ignore the sentences after it, and ignore what the word digest actually means in a biological context.</div> </div> </div> </div>The humor actually comes from a literal interpretation of Page 93 (RAW) instead of the spirit (RAI). Not from anything being taken out of context. However, I am going to bow out of the discussion because you are taking it in a really ugly direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T03:45:20-07:00","id":445557,"title":"","content":"As I understood it, Primal Urge 2 werewolf could eat a nice steak with creamy mushrom sauce and roasted potatoes (yum!) just fine. The thing is that he would get the same nourishment from that that if he had just eat the steak alone, everything else becames just waste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T04:24:48-07:00","id":445576,"title":"","content":"The reason they can't get nutrition from stuff is because they're becoming more like a wolf spirit. Therefore the reaction their body has to things other than what they can eat is also like that of a wolf spirit. It ignores it. It's not that the broccoli contains stuff you can't process. What's happening is that your body<i> \u200brefuses to acknowledge that it exists at all.</i><br /> <br /> How can you get sick from veggies you never ate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T06:06:30-07:00","id":445691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445576#post445576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can you get sick from veggies you never ate?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I never ate veggies, I suspect I'd get pretty sick! :-D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T06:38:04-07:00","id":445733,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but you're not a carnivore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T06:47:21-07:00","id":445741,"title":"","content":"We should all be glad that werewolves do not have the full &quot;feeding restrictions&quot; spirits have, because otherwise eating vegetables would turn a Werewolf into a vegetable/predator Magath. Bless Luna that Werewolves can only digest things that reinforce their resonance, and not things that could twist it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T08:09:38-07:00","id":445893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445441#post445441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not by definition, but it's going to be difficult for them to find other easy sources of essence. :-/</div> </div> </div> </div>Best option for them is to go into the spirit world, find a nice Locus to hold onto, and graze on its output. Frequently hunt small groups of low-ranked spirits and the occasional larger one getting too big for its britches.<br /> <br /> You'll be able to make it fine as long as nothing goes wrong. /tempting fate","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:36:52-07:00","id":446051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445545#post445545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is the biological aspects causing me to twitch with the implications? Yeah, but I'm probably not going to ever touch on it in an actual game. I'm not <i>that</i> crazy</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is the only, RAW, biological aspect implication is that werewolves that try to go vegetarian will starve to death; like any other obligate carnivore.<br /> <br /> If you want me to go into a much more thorough biological explanation I can back up with fully scientific analysis, I really can. But it seems pretty pointless. There's a very simple term for what you ingest, but don't digest: excrement. That's what happens to werewolves that eat vegetable matter. It turns into poo without providing nutrients to the bloodstream. It might even make their experience shitting nicer (that's why cats eat grass after all).<br /> <br /> There really isn't any reason for you to &quot;twitch&quot; about &quot;implications&quot; from a purely scientific perspective. Beyond the suspension of disbelief factor of dealing with werewolves here, animals all ingest things they don't/can't digest. It's pretty much a universal animal issue. Sometimes it's a bad thing, most of the time its a neutral thing, and sometimes it's a good thing. Indigestible does not equate to things that make you sick if you ingest them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eh, I would if I wanted to not include physical starvation as a part and parcel of the wolfy condition but I do see where you're coming from. </div> </div> </div>Physical starvation is part of the wolfy condition because werewolves are still living creatures that need to eat. The only difference is that PU 1 werewolves can stave off starvation using all the same food as humans, and PU 2+ werewolves have more restrictive diets.<br /> <br /> Unless you're taking out the need to eat completely (which seems like it would set off the biological implication twinge a lot harder...) physical starvation is always going to be a potential problem. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445549#post445549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The humor actually comes from a literal interpretation of Page 93 (RAW) instead of the spirit (RAI). Not from anything being taken out of context. However, I am going to bow out of the discussion because you are taking it in a really ugly direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>....<br /> <br /> 1) The literal interpretation of p. 93 is that werewolves can't digest non-meat. Digest means, literally, to break down ingested material into a form that can be absorbed into the body. Not being able to digest something does not literally mean it causes any sort of biological malfunction. As previously posted, animals purposefully ingest things they cannot digest all the time as <i>healthy</i> behavior.<br /> <br /> 2) Yes, you are taking it out of context as the book specifies &quot;obligate carnivores&quot; which is not &quot;animals that have severe gastrointestinal distress if they consume anything but meat,&quot; but rather, &quot;animals that have to consume meat to obtain their biological nutrients.&quot; Yes, you are skipping the next sentence that says, &quot;While she can ingest other foods she cannot gain nourishment from them,...&quot;<br /> <br /> 3) The only &quot;dark&quot; place I've taken this, is that humor is subjective. Going around insisting an a <b>incorrect</b> statement on the literal definition of digest, that leads to implications which have no actual backing in the RAW, just to make poop jokes is... not going to work for everyone. That's not dark. That's just basic truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T13:00:02-07:00","id":446412,"title":"","content":"How can werewolves have any pudding if they don't eat their meat???","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T13:53:39-07:00","id":446506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445433#post445433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> High PU werewolves have an increasingly restricted diet. It's part of the price they pay for being half spirit supernatural creatures. They're not human. They don't follow all human-understood scientific laws.<br /> <br /> They can eat other things, they don't gain sustenance from them. That's it. I think it's explained clearly on p 93.</div> </div> </div> </div><i><b>Bunyip</b></i>... I am curious...<br /> <br /> Why go the route of a Feeding Restriction (a mandate) instead of making it an aspect of Purity (a choice) as before? Not that it isn't an interesting decision, mind you. Why that particular route? Can you (or the member of the writing team that implemented that decision) discuss that at any length?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 03-17-2015, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T16:31:23-07:00","id":446680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=446051#post446051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is the only, RAW, biological aspect implication is that werewolves that try to go vegetarian will starve to death; like any other obligate carnivore.<br /> <br /> If you want me to go into a much more thorough biological explanation I can back up with fully scientific analysis, I really can. But it seems pretty pointless. There's a very simple term for what you ingest, but don't digest: excrement. That's what happens to werewolves that eat vegetable matter. It turns into poo without providing nutrients to the bloodstream. It might even make their experience shitting nicer (that's why cats eat grass after all).<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, thank you for the condescending tone and attempt to teach me about basic biology 101. I know what obligate carnivores are and how the acts of digestion and ingestion are different. However, before I made the thread, I did not know that the feeding restriction was a spiritual change upon the body and that they'd roughly kept the Uratha much like they had in Blood of the Wolf were the biological aspects were discussed.<br /> <br /> Which was why it piqued me when suddenly werewolves who were still essentially humans who turned into wolves with a bit of spirit voodoo tossed in suddenly lost the ability to ingest anything beyond meat and why is that seeing as our digestive system is designed to break down meat and beyond. Am I twitchy because it was a human digestive system that no longer functioned and why? Sure.<br /> <br /> People of a less confrontational nature than you answered me sufficently enough with the idea that 2ed Uratha weren't like their 1ed counterparts and while I still don't like the biological change from an omnivore diet to obligate carnivore - I can accept it with the handle of &quot;because we are actually focusing on the half-spirit trope now&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445576#post445576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason they can't get nutrition from stuff is because they're becoming more like a wolf spirit. Therefore the reaction their body has to things other than what they can eat is also like that of a wolf spirit. It ignores it. It's not that the broccoli contains stuff you can't process. What's happening is that your body<i> \u200brefuses to acknowledge that it exists at all.</i><br /> <br /> How can you get sick from veggies you never ate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. This works incredibly well for me to the point where everything now clicks and there's a lot of new, interesting implications that I can poke at in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":". 03-17-2015, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T16:49:38-07:00","id":446700,"title":"","content":"Glad I could be of assistance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T16:54:58-07:00","id":446709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=446680#post446680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...and how the acts of digestion and ingestion are different.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...suddenly lost the ability to ingest anything beyond meat... </div> </div> </div>When this is explicitly in the text not the case. They lost the ability to digest anything beyond meat while retaining the ability to ingest a wider variety of foods.<br /> <br /> You're getting snippy with me about pointing out the differences between these two things, when your initial reading/response seems based on confusing them together. You're still making statements that conflate the two. I'm glad the people going on the &quot;they're supernaturals&quot; thing did eventually work for you, but I didn't take that route because your initial posts expressed a lot of dissatisfaction with that explanation.<br /> <br /> As for tonal issues, please at least remember this is text. I didn't say anything mean or bad about you. You can put the judgmental stuff aside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T17:04:02-07:00","id":446720,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I am getting an unfortunate sense of d</span><span style=\"color:#223645\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u00e9j\u00e0 vu. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T17:04:39-07:00","id":446722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=446709#post446709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for tonal issues, please at least remember this is text. I didn't say anything mean or bad about you. You can put the judgmental stuff aside.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh? Because this: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want me to go into a much more thorough biological explanation I can back up with fully scientific analysis, I really can. But it seems pretty pointless</div> </div> </div> </div>Comes off as condescending. If you didn't intend that to be so, then that's where the disconnect is. If I am being seen as snippy towards you in return, it is because I've been filtering your responses as if they've been condescending at best and outright mocking at worst towards me.<br /> <br /> As for the confusion on my part: the book never gave reason as to why they were suddenly obligate carnivores. There's nothing in the Primal Urge section that goes: This is a spiritual thing subverting her physiological nature completely. Re-reading the section now, I do see that it does make the distinguishing between digestion and ingestion - I had read both as digestion.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T17:59:25-07:00","id":446817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=446722#post446722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the confusion on my part: the book never gave reason as to why they were suddenly obligate carnivores. There's nothing in the Primal Urge section that goes: This is a spiritual thing subverting her physiological nature completely.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's on page 94, right under Primal Urge. 'Primal Urge is the Uratha\u2019s innermost instinct; it\u2019s the fire inside that yearns to overwhelm, kill, and consume. To the wolf inside the Uratha, everything is pack, prey, mate, or territory. It sees everything in shades of meat.' Then as your Primal Urge increases, 'a werewolf sheds her human upbringing. She becomes closer to the Goddess of the Hunt, the ultimate predator.' That predator is Father Wolf, who is both spirit of the hunt, and of the wolf, so you become a carnivore like them. And after you hit a certain point you've shed so much of your human side that you gain no sustenance from food, only from the essence you can pull from bodies or raw essence from spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T00:51:20-07:00","id":447336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=446722#post446722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re-reading the section now, I do see that it does make the distinguishing between digestion and ingestion - I had read both as digestion.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, in that light, does my exacerbation and stress on that make a bit more sense as not intending to be condescending?<br /> <br /> Whatever filters you may feel my posts deserve, I'd wish that, &quot;Oh wait, I misread that, and that's why HA is going on about digestion vs. ingestion so much,&quot; would be enough to get a re-reading without those filters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T01:15:11-07:00","id":447370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=446506#post446506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i><b>Bunyip</b></i>... I am curious...<br /> <br /> Why go the route of a Feeding Restriction (a mandate) instead of making it an aspect of Purity (a choice) as before? Not that it isn't an interesting decision, mind you. Why that particular route? Can you (or the member of the writing team that implemented that decision) discuss that at any length?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in detail, no - it wasn't part of my assignment. From memory, I think it was the developer's decision, but could be wrong. (We did write this thing over 12 months ago!)<br /> <br /> But that said, what nofather wrote (below) is why as I understand it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=446817#post446817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's on page 94, right under Primal Urge. 'Primal Urge is the Uratha\u2019s innermost instinct; it\u2019s the fire inside that yearns to overwhelm, kill, and consume. To the wolf inside the Uratha, everything is pack, prey, mate, or territory. It sees everything in shades of meat.' Then as your Primal Urge increases, 'a werewolf sheds her human upbringing. She becomes closer to the Goddess of the Hunt, the ultimate predator.' That predator is Father Wolf, who is both spirit of the hunt, and of the wolf, so you become a carnivore like them. And after you hit a certain point you've shed so much of your human side that you gain no sustenance from food, only from the essence you can pull from bodies or raw essence from spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T04:17:07-07:00","id":447478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=447336#post447336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, in that light, does my exacerbation and stress on that make a bit more sense as not intending to be condescending?<br /> <br /> Whatever filters you may feel my posts deserve, I'd wish that, &quot;Oh wait, I misread that, and that's why HA is going on about digestion vs. ingestion so much,&quot; would be enough to get a re-reading without those filters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be honest, no, because even if my mistake was simple reading miscomprehension at 5am in the morning, the way you responded made me feel like an idiot for even asking the question on the forums - even if it stemmed from a silly misread. No reconsideration of your point of view can change that fact.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-18T07:46:19-07:00","id":447672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=447370#post447370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not in detail, no - it wasn't part of my assignment. From memory, I think it was the developer's decision, but could be wrong. (We did write this thing over 12 months ago!)<br /> <br /> But that said, what nofather wrote (below) is why as I understand it.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhh... Thanks <i><b>Bunyip (</b></i>and <i><b>Nofather) </b></i>for the clarification. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T03:30:50-07:00","id":448974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445535#post445535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you mean the Primal Urge 8-10 Uratha have Essence restriction, they should be able to eat spirits also. You just need to call the <i>Siskur-Dah</i> every day to eat some spirits. Yes, <i>Hisil</i> will hate high PU werewolves...</div> </div> </div> </div>Also why Uratha no longer are spirit cops.. They have high PU going on hunts for sustenance in Hisil.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T03:40:06-07:00","id":448978,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, you have the rank 0 &quot;treated like fruit&quot; spirits to hunt if you want. <br /> <br /> And you can declare siskur-dah on pretty much ''anything''<br /> <br /> So you can have a high PU wolf be all &quot;Siskur-Dah!&quot; *pulls out fishing rod*<br /> <br /> Also I think it's been said that feeding from loci counts too. And can involve actual eating now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T03:41:20-07:00","id":448979,"title":"","content":"I can see why some people take this as a joke. That is OK with me.<br /> <br /> Werewolf sustenance makes just as much sense as a game about vampires feeding.<br /> <b>It is a role-playing game.</b> Reality was left at the door when you entered this realm of weirdness.<br /> <br /> It is pretty clear from the texts in the core book how a Werewolf feeds.<br /> Sustenance needs become more harsher to balance the power that stems from being a high PU Werewolf.<br /> This creates a lot of fun gaming stuff to use.<br /> <br /> I for one have already added a high PU lone wolf cannibal as an antagonist in our game.<br /> <br /> Feeding has yet to be a problem in our game. Then again, our game is set in the state of Wyoming. Lots of four legged food!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T08:46:01-07:00","id":449311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=448978#post448978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, you have the rank 0 &quot;treated like fruit&quot; spirits to hunt if you want.<br /> <br /> And you can declare siskur-dah on pretty much ''anything''<br /> <br /> So you can have a high PU wolf be all &quot;Siskur-Dah!&quot; *pulls out fishing rod*<br /> <br /> Also I think it's been said that feeding from loci counts too. And can involve actual eating now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stew's already said that it's not as neat as that, and that aving a high-PU werewolf in the area is going to quickly destabilize the (spiritual) environment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T15:13:27-07:00","id":450924,"title":"","content":"Since I didn't see it mentioned yet, a werewolf can use a Devourer's Fang fetish to circumvent the feeding restrictions of high Primal Urge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T15:32:14-07:00","id":450943,"title":"","content":"I myself would house-rule that Werewolves can digest other foods but have a mild reaction to it, like lactose-intolerance that worsens with age. Before long the only hunger for and gain satisfaction from meat and they start to prefer their stakes rare until anything but raw meat won't slake that hunger, from something that fought back. Eventually even meat just doesn't set right and only essence nourishes the body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","user":"Xaielao","date":". 03-20-2015, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T16:21:00-07:00","id":450971,"title":"","content":"For those who mentioned other animals eating things they can't digest normally, and it sometimes helping their digestive track? This is nothing compared to that.<br /> This is almost every single food you can imagine not being digestible. This is the kind of specialized diet that everyone is going to notice. This is the lowest carb diet you could ever imagine. This is Atkins taken up to 11. Hell, your situation actually improves once you can eat carnivores and essence.<br /> <br /> But yeah. Don't worry about it in game. Just handwave it away as spirit magic or something.<br /> And for those that are really concerned about primal urge food restrictions? Devourer's Fang fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T17:41:28-07:00","id":451108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=450971#post450971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those who mentioned other animals eating things they can't digest normally, and it sometimes helping their digestive track? This is nothing compared to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm. It compares to that in the sometimes when it isn't an aid. A good number of predators swallow their prey whole, for example, and have to vomit up things like bones that they can't pass through their stomachs (owls being a common example as pellets are often examined in classrooms). Something Uratha don't have to put up with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is the kind of specialized diet that everyone is going to notice. </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't, because you can still ingest and excrete food you can't digest. A werewolf that has a salad isn't going to have any external sign that it didn't do anything for them in terms of nourishment. If you want to eat raw meat in public? Have some carpaccio, crudo, tartare, etc. There's plenty of raw meat dishes out there. It isn't until you're at PU 6 and you're on eating carnivores only (and then depends on how your group feels about fish and that counting given how many common food fish are carnivores; 'cause sushi) that you're going to get a bit more noticeable.<br /> <br /> And... that's assuming you even eat in public on a regular basis. Lots of people raise their own livestock, or hunt, giving them lots of access to meat that they can eat at home with their pack. Who's going to notice that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T18:03:22-07:00","id":451119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=445733#post445733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but you're not a carnivore.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My bad, that was unclear. I was joking, because I could get sick from a lack of veggies, which, in a sense, would be getting sick from veggies I didn't eat.<br /> <br /> Also, 3 pages of posts ago necro!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T18:37:21-07:00","id":451165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451108#post451108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erm. It compares to that in the sometimes when it isn't an aid. A good number of predators swallow their prey whole, for example, and have to vomit up things like bones that they can't pass through their stomachs (owls being a common example as pellets are often examined in classrooms). Something Uratha don't have to put up with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting aside spirit magic as the handwave answer? Uratha who maintain anything resembling an ordinary human diet would blow away owls and snakes in the quantity of food they have to expel from their bodies, not to mention those creatures are capable of digesting a much wider range of material than an Uratha between PU2 and PU5.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451108#post451108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it isn't, because you can still ingest and excrete food you can't digest. A werewolf that has a salad isn't going to have any external sign that it didn't do anything for them in terms of nourishment. If you want to eat raw meat in public? Have some carpaccio, crudo, tartare, etc. There's plenty of raw meat dishes out there. It isn't until you're at PU 6 and you're on eating carnivores only (and then depends on how your group feels about fish and that counting given how many common food fish are carnivores; 'cause sushi) that you're going to get a bit more noticeable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting aside spirit magic as the handwave answer? If you're ingesting that much material, it's going to come back out one way or another, and anybody who spends more than a little time with you is going to notice. There are also the roleplay implications. It might cause gas. It might cause indigestion. It might cause cramping. It might cause bloating. It might cause bowel obstructions. It might cause nausea. There is a huge list of reasons why it could be simply uncomfortable to eat a regular person diet. People and animals alike have tons of issues with food they probably shouldn't eat, and none of them are even remotely as restrictive as a werewolf.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451108#post451108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And... that's assuming you even eat in public on a regular basis. Lots of people raise their own livestock, or hunt, giving them lots of access to meat that they can eat at home with their pack. Who's going to notice that?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are hanging out in the woods, then you're right. You're not going to have many problems. But eating is one of the biggest ways our species spends time together. Haven't seen your brother in a while? Let's go out to eat! Hanging out with your friends on friday? Let's hit the bar! Your workplace bought pizza for lunch today! The business meeting is over lunch today! People who are not your pack are going to notice sooner or later.<br /> <br /> That's why its best to handwave the whole thing as solved by spirit magic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T19:00:32-07:00","id":451179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451165#post451165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uratha who maintain anything resembling an ordinary human diet would blow away owls and snakes in the quantity of food they have to expel from their bodies, not to mention those creatures are capable of digesting a much wider range of material than an Uratha between PU2 and PU5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most owls, and most snakes, can only digest meat... In the wild they only eat raw meat as well. That's the same restrictions as Uratha.<br /> <br /> As for the amount they need to expel? Sure. If they eat a lot of things they can't digest, it's turned into poop. Fortunately humans are weird and hate pooping in front of each other. Some people just like to take their time on the can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are also the roleplay implications. It might cause gas. It might cause indigestion. It might cause cramping. It might cause bloating. It might cause bowel obstructions. It might cause nausea. There is a huge list of reasons why it could be simply uncomfortable to eat a regular person diet. </div> </div> </div>It could. But the books don't say that it does.... so why should it? These things are not a necessity of the RAW. They're implications that you're suggesting. If you want to run them? Cool. But they're not a default in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you are hanging out in the woods, then you're right. You're not going to have many problems. But eating is one of the biggest ways our species spends time together. Haven't seen your brother in a while? Let's go out to eat! Hanging out with your friends on friday? Let's hit the bar! Your workplace bought pizza for lunch today! The business meeting is over lunch today! People who are not your pack are going to notice sooner or later. </div> </div> </div>Fortunately, the 2e rules have vastly expanded who can be in your pack. Your brother is easily another Uratha or Wolf-Blooded if they're still around. The friends you go to the bar with are absolutely your pack. Workplace and business meetings... aren't something more werewolves worry about.<br /> <br /> And yes, werewolves have trouble with normal human social activities. The fact that they can flip out and murder people over a seemingly minor faux pas generally being a bigger deal than their diet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why its best to handwave the whole thing as solved by spirit magic. </div> </div> </div>The problem I have with this is that you're basically forcing things in that aren't actually there... just to have to hand wave them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T19:30:11-07:00","id":451192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451179#post451179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most owls, and most snakes, can only digest meat... In the wild they only eat raw meat as well. That's the same restrictions as Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can partially digest a wide variety of things, including oils and trace minerals. Some things they can digest but not absorb, which aids in creating feces which facilitates the expulsion of material they definitely cannot digest. It entirely depends on how resistant the swallowed material is to a given animals PH level / relevant enzymes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451179#post451179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the amount they need to expel? Sure. If they eat a lot of things they can't digest, it's turned into poop. Fortunately humans are weird and hate pooping in front of each other. Some people just like to take their time on the can.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that easy, because their bodies would not be able to partially digest a huge number of materials and create feces that would facilitate bowel movements. They would be especially prone to obstructions and intestinal shredding due to undigested material. They can easily heal that, but I seriously doubt it would be pleasant. As for making frequent or prolonged trips to the bathroom, people notice that as well.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451179#post451179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could. But the books don't say that it does.... so why should it? These things are not a necessity of the RAW. They're implications that you're suggesting. If you want to run them? Cool. But they're not a default in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to run them. That's why saying it should be handwaved away as solved by spirit magic.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451179#post451179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fortunately, the 2e rules have vastly expanded who can be in your pack. Your brother is easily another Uratha or Wolf-Blooded if they're still around. The friends you go to the bar with are absolutely your pack. Workplace and business meetings... aren't something more werewolves worry about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other Uratha are hopefully not going to be a problem, but the world involves interacting with a lot more people that just other Uratha, unless you're the intentional recluse mentioned before. And intentional recluses definitely draw attention, especially in the world of darkness. As for wolf-blooded, that brings the same kind of issues as trusting any NPC with your secrets. It's a plot ripe for any storyteller to plunder for stories.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451179#post451179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem I have with this is that you're basically forcing things in that aren't actually there... just to have to hand wave them.</div> </div> </div> </div>We both agree it shouldn't be done, just for different reasons. Right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T20:59:17-07:00","id":451265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451192#post451192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can partially digest a wide variety of things, including oils and trace minerals. Some things they can digest but not absorb, which aids in creating feces which facilitates the expulsion of material they definitely cannot digest. It entirely depends on how resistant the swallowed material is to a given animals PH level / relevant enzymes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're parsing this a bit off.<br /> <br /> First off &quot;digest&quot; biologically means, &quot;process so it can be absorbed.&quot; Something you can &quot;digest but not absorb&quot; only occurs if you consume so much you can't absorb it effectively, or there's something else getting in the way. Processing things like fiber to aid excretion is not digestion.<br /> <br /> Second, the book says &quot;meat.&quot; It does not get into details on nutrients and macromolecules. Meat is tissue that contains proteins, enzymes, minerals, lipids, vitamins, carbohydrates, and so on. Claiming that Uratha (at least until they need Essence) can't absorb oils or trace minerals doesn't add up because those things are part of meat tissues. The marbling on a steak isn't fat added to meat. It is part of that cut of meat. When a wolf eats a deer's liver, it gets a big hit of iron and vitamins from that organ meat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not that easy, because their bodies would not be able to partially digest a huge number of materials and create feces that would facilitate bowel movements. </div> </div> </div>Why not? The book doesn't say this. The book says it can't get nourishment from those materials, not that the Uratha's stomach doesn't have effective gastric juices to break apart materials. It says they can't absorb anything that's not meat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other Uratha are hopefully not going to be a problem, but the world involves interacting with a lot more people that just other Uratha, unless you're the intentional recluse mentioned before. </div> </div> </div>There's a big difference between &quot;interacting&quot; and &quot;constantly being around enough for people to bother paying attention to your bathroom habits.&quot; Uratha are written as being fairly reclusive from mainstream human society as is. The descriptions of packs in 2e are things like gangs, or tight knit police units; the people you spend your day-to-day with are your pack. You're not an office worker during the day that goes to be with the pack at night.<br /> <br /> Though running around in Hishu does that the advantage of penalizing attempts to notice you being out of place in the crowd. A mid-range PU Uratha is going to have most minor quirks covered up by their human form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for wolf-blooded, that brings the same kind of issues as trusting any NPC with your secrets. It's a plot ripe for any storyteller to plunder for stories. </div> </div> </div>Sure. But it's also presented as the default of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We both agree it shouldn't be done, just for different reasons. Right? </div> </div> </div>Yep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T21:54:40-07:00","id":451292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451265#post451265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not an office worker during the day that goes to be with the pack at night.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could be, though. Nothing says you have to eschew human civilization. In fact part of the Oath of the Moon strongly suggests you don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T00:49:19-07:00","id":451361,"title":"","content":"You could try... mechanically speaking the results would be pretty messy. You're exposing yourself to a lot of sins towards the Flesh during the day; even if you balance it out at night with your pack. It would be pretty easy for a long stressful day at the office to push you too far towards the Flesh that you pretty much screwed if a Trigger comes up. <br /> <br /> And the Oath of the Moon doesn't really weigh in on civilization or being part of mainstream culture. It simply says to keep humans as part of your life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T02:21:34-07:00","id":451383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451361#post451361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're exposing yourself to a lot of sins towards the Flesh during the day</div> </div> </div> </div>Like what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T03:14:02-07:00","id":451390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451265#post451265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a big difference between &quot;interacting&quot; and &quot;constantly being around enough for people to bother paying attention to your bathroom habits.&quot; Uratha are written as being fairly reclusive from mainstream human society as is. The descriptions of packs in 2e are things like gangs, or tight knit police units; the people you spend your day-to-day with are your pack. You're not an office worker during the day that goes to be with the pack at night.<br /> <br /> Though running around in Hishu does that the advantage of penalizing attempts to notice you being out of place in the crowd. A mid-range PU Uratha is going to have most minor quirks covered up by their human form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that &quot;living human life by day&quot; is <i>totally</i> new Iron Masters thing. And the Pack based on the office workers working for their Alpha CEO. I got very much Glasswalkers vibe from the Iron Masters now - you are werewolves that dear to show other Uratha that &quot;yes, WE CAN DO IT!&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Company, many times, is as much tight group, as families or gang can be,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T08:47:24-07:00","id":451561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451383#post451383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eating processed food is a good example. Since pretty much all the food you're going to have access to that you don't bring yourself in most offices is going to be such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451390#post451390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue that &quot;living human life by day&quot; is <i>totally</i> new Iron Masters thing. And the Pack based on the office workers working for their Alpha CEO.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I can absolutely see. Though it gets around most of the reasons this example was brought up. An Uratha working in an Iron Master front business with the majority (if not all) of the workers part of the pack gets around any possible issues of people noticing/caring about some of the employees having odd eating/pooping issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T08:57:47-07:00","id":451581,"title":"","content":"Processed food is only an issue if you're harmony is 3 or less. And that should probably actually be 2 or less because of symmetry but whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T09:30:51-07:00","id":451609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451581#post451581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Processed food is only an issue if you're harmony is 3 or less. And that should probably actually be 2 or less because of symmetry but whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and death rage triggers aren't something you have to worry about unless you're an office worker in a silver knife making company or you specifically chose something common. Few of the examples would affect you in a day to day job. An office job is perfectly fine for a werewolf, and it probably makes for a great Physical Touchstone. Not everyone who becomes a werewolf leaves their entire life behind and becomes an aimless drifter. There's still things like the Eigner Lodge, which operates as a dream research clinic in Vienna, and the Lodge of the Shield who are police officers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T10:16:54-07:00","id":451695,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how much I want to arguing this, especially as it has gotten severely off topic, but the Harmony sins list isn't supposed to be exhaustive. &quot;Breaking points toward Flesh involve actively denying her Uratha nature.&quot; Trying to maintain a human life is exactly that.<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to say that every day at work you have good odds of flipping out. I'm saying that 8+ hours a day, 5 days a week, 50ish weeks a year, a few days of overtime? All it takes is one bad day out of those to end up getting Triggered. And this is a pretty standard part of the source material that in the end this sort of thing ends bad.<br /> <br /> The whole point of this tangent was, again, that &quot;odd digestive issues&quot; is by far a lesser concern than others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T10:36:13-07:00","id":451713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451390#post451390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would argue that &amp;quot;living human life by day&amp;quot; is <i>totally</i> new Iron Masters thing. And the Pack based on the office workers working for their Alpha CEO. I got very much Glasswalkers vibe from the Iron Masters now - you are werewolves that dear to show other Uratha that &amp;quot;yes, WE CAN DO IT!&amp;quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Company, many times, is as much tight group, as families or gang can be,</div> </div> </div> </div>I think &quot;The Company&quot; would make an awesome physical Touchstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T10:45:17-07:00","id":451750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451695#post451695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how much I want to arguing this, especially as it has gotten severely off topic, but the Harmony sins list isn't supposed to be exhaustive. &quot;Breaking points toward Flesh involve actively denying her Uratha nature.&quot; Trying to maintain a human life is exactly that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a job isn't denying their Uratha nature. It's having a job. Nothing keeps them from embracing their Uratha nature after work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not trying to say that every day at work you have good odds of flipping out. I'm saying that 8+ hours a day, 5 days a week, 50ish weeks a year, a few days of overtime? All it takes is one bad day out of those to end up getting Triggered. And this is a pretty standard part of the source material that in the end this sort of thing ends bad. </div> </div> </div>Except for the many werewolves who do have jobs. And it doesn't matter how bad your day is unless that's your trigger. For a whole class of triggers, you're completely fine as long as you don't work in a Wound.<br /> <br /> The odd digestive issues point was answered a long time ago, but your argument against it having no impact on people because werewolves don't have jobs or hang around normal people is something not supported by the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T11:24:32-07:00","id":451804,"title":"","content":"I mean, werewolves do tend to spend more time around their Packmates than anyone else, and honestly a guy who eats a lot of rare meat and spends a lot of time in the bathroom is really not that weird. The conclusion most people would probably come to (if they even noticed) is either food poisoning from all the rare meat, or IBS, neither of which are going to cause any significant social problems for the Uratha if his coworkers make that assumption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-21-2015, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-21T11:35:55-07:00","id":451828,"title":"","content":"For the Costanza-minded werewolves, you could use a gift of warding to ensure privacy in one of the nicer restrooms in the building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T02:46:44-07:00","id":452444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451265#post451265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off &quot;digest&quot; biologically means, &quot;process so it can be absorbed.&quot; Something you can &quot;digest but not absorb&quot; only occurs if you consume so much you can't absorb it effectively, or there's something else getting in the way. Processing things like fiber to aid excretion is not digestion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was intentionally avoiding including absorption in the definition, because that way lies madness! <u>You just eliminated water.</u><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451265#post451265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, the book says &quot;meat.&quot; It does not get into details on nutrients and macromolecules. Meat is tissue that contains proteins, enzymes, minerals, lipids, vitamins, carbohydrates, and so on. Claiming that Uratha (at least until they need Essence) can't absorb oils or trace minerals doesn't add up because those things are part of meat tissues. The marbling on a steak isn't fat added to meat. It is part of that cut of meat. When a wolf eats a deer's liver, it gets a big hit of iron and vitamins from that organ meat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can get behind this without issue. It does create the question of whether or not a Werewolf can gain nourishment from protein, vitamin, oil, herbal, or medicinal supplements that are not delivered via meat digestion.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451265#post451265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not? The book doesn't say this. The book says it can't get nourishment from those materials, not that the Uratha's stomach doesn't have effective gastric juices to break apart materials. It says they can't absorb anything that's not meat.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't tease me earlier about assuming biological functions that aren't written in the book, and then turn around and assume biological functions that are not written in the book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=451265#post451265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a big difference between &quot;interacting&quot; and &quot;constantly being around enough for people to bother paying attention to your bathroom habits.&quot; Uratha are written as being fairly reclusive from mainstream human society as is. The descriptions of packs in 2e are things like gangs, or tight knit police units; the people you spend your day-to-day with are your pack. You're not an office worker during the day that goes to be with the pack at night.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this has been sufficiently poked at by other posters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2447,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","user":"TwitchTheRat","date":". 03-22-2015, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T13:08:24-07:00","id":453067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwitchTheRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/445315-primal-urge-re-feeding-restriction?p=452444#post452444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can get behind this without issue. It does create the question of whether or not a Werewolf can gain nourishment from protein, vitamin, oil, herbal, or medicinal supplements that are not delivered via meat digestion.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually what caused me to poke at the entire issue in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}